Both functions now contain the identical five-line shape:
  const p = args.particulars as Record<string, unknown>;
  const particulars = Object.keys(p)
    .sort()
    .map((k) => `${k}=${JSON.stringify(p[k] ?? null)}`)
    .join(",");
grep -n "Object.keys(p)" apps/web/lib/registers/fixed-assets.ts returns exactly these two hits, both in this one file. completeIntent's own doc comment even says '...the same convention reviseIntent below uses,' naming the duplication it is choosing to repeat rather than share.
